  <h3>How is information sent on the web via HTTP?</h3>
  <p>
    An HTTP request is done when you send a link through a browser, that then
    asks a dns for where the server is and then it routes the request. Then
    the server sends a response with all the files for your
    web page, unless you have them cached in your browser or DNS.
  </p>
  <h3>What is semantic meaning in HTML?</h3>
  <p>
    HTML is hypertext and that means its better than text because there is extra
    meaning to the plain text. That is semantics. Semantics give extra meaning
    and structure to HTML.
  </p>
  <h3>What are CSS selectors?</h3>
  <p>
    CSS is a stylesheet. Its job is to change the look of an HTML. It can
    change:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Colors</li>
    <li>Images</li>
    <li>Layout</li>
    <li>Transitions</li>
    <li>Animations</li>
    <li>Interactions</li>
  </ul>
